fsck - check a Project9 filesystem image

SYNOPSIS
    build/fsck [image]
    make fsck [FS_IMAGE=image]

DESCRIPTION
    Check a Project9 filesystem image from the build host. The
    default image is fs.img. Stop the guest before checking a disk.

    fsck checks the superblock, journal, inodes, directories, block
    ownership, allocation bitmap, and link counts. It applies valid
    committed journal records to its copy in memory. The image is
    opened read-only.

EXIT STATUS
    0   The filesystem is clean.
    1   The filesystem contains an inconsistency.
    2   Usage or I/O error.

SEE ALSO
    stability(1)
